WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.000
Lesson 8.11 · Marketing & Communications
Media relations and press materials

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.800
When nobody knows you yet, a launch or first result can be a local story worth telling.

3
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:25.911
Media relations means building relationships with journalists so they cover your work. Coverage builds credibility and reaches people you could not reach alone, which matters when nobody knows you yet.

4
00:00:26.311 --> 00:00:26.911
Getting ready for the media

5
00:00:26.911 --> 00:00:36.759
A newsworthy angle: Timely, local, human stories with evidence and people willing to speak. For example: Local radio covers the bakery’s first trainees finishing their six months.

6
00:00:36.759 --> 00:00:47.348
Press kit: Short and long descriptions, facts, founder biographies, consented photos, logos and contacts. For example: Two pages and a photo folder, ready to send in a minute.

7
00:00:47.348 --> 00:00:57.656
Spokespeople: Agreed people who speak, with key messages prepared. For example: Only the two founders speak; trainees appear only with consent and support.

8
00:00:58.056 --> 00:00:58.656
Why it matters

9
00:00:58.656 --> 00:01:03.589
1. Coverage builds credibility when you have no track record.

10
00:01:03.589 --> 00:01:08.893
2. Local outlets often reach your audiences better than national ones.

11
00:01:08.893 --> 00:01:14.456
3. Preparation protects participants and keeps your messages clear.

12
00:01:14.856 --> 00:01:15.456
When you will use it

13
00:01:15.456 --> 00:01:19.278
1. Your launch and your first results.

14
00:01:19.278 --> 00:01:23.470
2. Alongside your messaging framework and proof points.

15
00:01:23.470 --> 00:01:29.404
3. Your crisis plan: who speaks if something goes wrong.

16
00:01:29.804 --> 00:01:30.404
What to avoid

17
00:01:30.404 --> 00:01:35.337
Mass mailing journalists instead of building a few relationships.

18
00:01:35.337 --> 00:01:41.381
Putting a participant in front of the media without consent and support.

19
00:01:41.381 --> 00:01:46.574
Promising results you have not yet achieved.

20
00:01:47.174 --> 00:01:48.974
You prepare your press kit checklist and first media list.

21
00:01:48.974 --> 00:01:52.974
Then save it, and download it as a PDF.

22
00:01:54.474 --> 00:01:57.574
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
